<% page_title "Before you sign in" %>

<%# The public demo's terms, shown in place of the sign-in form until the visitor accepts them (#952).
    A plain page and a form, so it works with no JavaScript and reads in order.
    Keep it consistent with the full terms at Configuration#demo_terms_url. %>
<div class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-xl">
  <div class="card">
    <h1>Before you sign in</h1>
    <p>
      This is a public demonstration.
      Please read these terms; signing in means you agree to them.
    </p>

    <ul
      id="demo-terms"
      class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5"
    >
      <li>
        <strong>It is a test system, with synthetic data only.</strong>
        Every patient in it is made up, and it is not used for care.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Never enter real patient information.</strong>
        That includes your own, a family member's, or anyone else's.
        Anyone can sign in with the published sign-in pairs, so others can see and change what you enter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No promise of uptime or of keeping data.</strong>
        It may be slow, down, or changed without notice.
        It is reset from time to time, and anything entered is erased.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Feedback goes in GitHub issues.</strong>
        <a href="<%= Lakeraven::EHR.configuration.demo_feedback_url %>">Open an issue</a>, and leave out anything about a real person.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4">
      <a href="<%= Lakeraven::EHR.configuration.demo_terms_url %>">Read the full terms of use</a>.
    </p>

    <%= form_with url: accept_demo_terms_path,
          method: :post,
          local: true,
          class: "mt-6" do %>
      <button
        type="submit"
        class="w-full"
      >I accept these terms</button>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
